---
---
<section id="work" class="bg-neutral-950 text-neutral-50 px-6 py-24">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">

    <div class="max-w-2xl mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Selected work</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-neutral-400">
        Three projects built for a single independent hotel, covering the guest-facing site, the numbers behind it, and the operations that keep it running.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-20">

      <!-- Case 1: Hotel website -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center border-t border-neutral-800 pt-12">
        <img
          src="/images/hotel-website.png"
          alt="Screenshot of the hotel booking website"
          class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-800 w-full"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="text-amber-400 font-medium text-sm mb-2">Guest-facing website</p>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">A booking site that converts, not just informs</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Designed and built the hotel's public website — room listings, live availability, and a direct booking flow that keeps commission in-house instead of going through third-party listing sites.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-300 border-l-2 border-amber-400 pl-3">
            Handles direct bookings across four room types without going through an OTA.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Case 2: Analytics app -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center border-t border-neutral-800 pt-12">
        <img
          src="/images/analytics-app.png"
          alt="Screenshot of the revenue analytics dashboard"
          class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-800 w-full md:order-2"
        />
        <div class="md:order-1">
          <p class="text-amber-400 font-medium text-sm mb-2">Revenue analytics app</p>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Every number a manager used to wait for month-end to see</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            Built a dashboard that tracks performance down to the individual room: revenue per booking, per room type, per day. What used to live in scattered spreadsheets is now one live view.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-300 border-l-2 border-amber-400 pl-3">
            Reports daily revenue per room type — down to what a single booking generates.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Case 3: Ops app -->
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center border-t border-neutral-800 pt-12">
        <img
          src="/images/ops-app.png"
          alt="Screenshot of the internal operations app"
          class="rounded-lg border border-neutral-800 w-full"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="text-amber-400 font-medium text-sm mb-2">Internal operations tool</p>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The tool the front desk actually opens every morning</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed">
            An internal app for day-to-day running of the hotel — housekeeping status, check-in/check-out tracking, and task handoffs between shifts, replacing paper logs.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-neutral-300 border-l-2 border-amber-400 pl-3">
            Used daily by front-desk and housekeeping staff to coordinate handoffs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>